critiques have emerged, arguing that the pursuit of AGI is often driven by normative frameworks rooted in historical 
eugenicist ideologies, which can lead to discriminatory outcomes and centralized power under the guise of safety and 
universal benefit [^10.5210_fm.v29i4.13636].                                                                         
+                                                                                                                    
+## Theoretical Foundations and Architectural Approaches                                                             
+On the theoretical front, researchers are exploring novel mathematical and topological frameworks to define the     
transition from computation to genuine autonomy. One recent treatise proposes replacing the subjective unit with a   
"Form F" as the primary constituent of mind, establishing a rigorous morphogenetic structure that demonstrates the   
mathematical inevitability of AGI through topological integrity and structural tension [^10.5281_zenodo.19034234].   
+                                                                                                                    
+## Safety, Verification, and Global Research Landscapes                                                             
+Ensuring the controllability of AGI remains a paramount challenge. Recent work advocates for a path to safe AGI     
grounded in formal verification and mechanistic interpretability, arguing that provably satisfying human-specified   
requirements is the only viable route to controllable superintelligence [^10.48550_arxiv.2309.01933]. Furthermore,   
tracking the global trajectory of AGI development reveals significant state-level investments, such as China's       
national strategy to lead in general AI by 2030, which involves monitoring dozens of institutions working on machine 
learning, brain-inspired AI, and brain-computer interfaces [^10.51593_20210064].                                     
                                                                                                                     

